      "message": "No we don\u0027t need that flag anymore. I had started to put together a lot of cleanup there: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/919698 but this never landed because I had to hack in `SK_AVOID_SLOW_RASTER_PIPELINE_BLURS` for chrome.  \n\nAs part of removing that hack, I started to implement a new blur algorithm variant for the raster pipeline that could apply color type conversion and a more accurate algorithm for small kernels. This would significantly impact the linked CL\u0027s changes in SkBlurEngine.cpp.  But I don\u0027t think there\u0027s any reason we couldn\u0027t land everything else from that CL and revisit the blur algorithm update separately.",
